from _w import w

w(436, "Built and tested this round. The owner opened Connections and found one new card, Google Maps, with a single box for the API key and a Test button, and a note saying which two Google services must be on (Geocoding and Distance Matrix). The restaurant settings got a button that finds the restaurant's place from its written address. With a key pasted, the by-the-kilometre charge uses real road distance from Google; with none, or when Google does not answer, it falls back to the earlier estimate and says so.",
 ["Connections has a Google Maps card with one required box (API key), the help text that names the Geocoding API and the Distance Matrix API, a Switch on tick, Test or Live, and a Try button; the key is stored encrypted and never shown again",
  "The restaurant's settings have an address box and Find it from the address above, which fills in the place; the order form and the menu page say whether the distance is by road (Google) or an estimate (straight line times the road allowance)",
  "Each order keeps whether its distance was by road or estimated (food_orders.distance_by_road); a road distance is kept for 7 days for the same two places, so the same trip is not asked for twice",
  "When Google is off, has no key, refuses the key, is slow or sends something unreadable, the order carries on with the estimate and nothing breaks (11 automatic tests with Google's replies simulated)",
  "The Try button on the card asks Google for one real address and one real distance and says in words which of the two worked"],
 [{"file": "f436_1.jpg", "caption": "The Google Maps card in Connections: one key box, the two services it needs, Test and Try", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/connections"}],
 ["Built this round after the owner asked that every outside service be code-complete so only a key is left to paste. Item 435's estimate stays as the fallback. NOT verified live: the call to Google itself, because there was no Google key and no network permission here; the code was checked against simulated Google answers (success, no route, denied key, timeout, bad reply). The first real key may need the Distance Matrix API switched on in the Google Cloud project, which is what the card's help text says."])

w(608, "Built and tested this round. The owner opened Connections and found two new cards under Visitor statistics and ads: Facebook (Meta) Pixel and Google Analytics. A Pixel ID and a Measurement ID were typed, the cards were switched on and set to Live, and the public site was then loaded.",
 ["Both cards ask for one number only and say where to find it; a Pixel ID must be 10 to 20 digits and a Measurement ID must look like G-ABC123XYZ4, anything else is refused with a plain reason (so nothing odd can be placed in the page)",
  "Nothing is sent until the card is on and set to Live; in Test mode, or switched off, the public page carries no tracking code at all",
  "Once Live, every public page loads the tags, and the site reports page views, product views, adds to cart, searches and orders; staff, the owner and the admin screens are never counted",
  "Google Analytics is told not to count its own page view because the app sends them as the page changes, so one visit is not counted twice",
  "The Test button answers without sending anything (12 automatic tests)"],
 [{"file": "f608_1.jpg", "caption": "Connections: the Pixel ID and the Measurement ID cards, both on and Live", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/connections"}],
 ["Built this round. NOT verified live: whether Meta or Google actually receive and show the events, because that needs the owner's real ids and their dashboards; the page code and the events were checked in the app and in 12 automatic tests. While fixing it a bug was found where a key containing a digit (analytics:ga4) could not be saved from the screen; fixed and covered by a test."])

w(609, "Built and tested this round, in two halves. Bulk texts: the owner opened Bulk texts, chose pharmacies as the audience, saw at once how many people would get it (5, 2 texts each, 10 in all, against a daily limit of 2,000), wrote an Eid offer and sent it. Affiliates: the owner made a promoter called Rima with a 3 percent share and the link /a/RIMA3; an order placed through the link was counted and a payout was written down.",
 ["Bulk texts: the audience can be narrowed by type (public, pharmacy, wholesale), tier, area, days since the last order and whether they owe us; before sending, the screen says how many will get it, how many texts each, how many in all and how many of today's limit are used",
  "Every text ends with a line to stop the messages (a link that works without signing in); anyone who stops is left out next time, and a person who opted out never gets another campaign text",
  "The campaign page lists each person (number hidden except the last digits) with sent, failed or waiting; it can be stopped, and started again where it stopped; the sending speed and the daily limit are settings",
  "Affiliates: the promoter's page shows the link, visits, orders and what has been earned and paid; the share applies to finished orders only and comes back off on a return or cancellation; the link leaves a code on the visitor's phone for the number of days set in Settings, and a buyer is never their own promoter's customer",
  "A payout pays what is owed in full, is written down with how it was paid (cash, bKash, Nagad, Rocket or bank) and a note, and is refused when nothing is owed (23 and 21 automatic tests)"],
 [{"file": "f609_1.jpg", "caption": "A new campaign: who gets it and how many texts that is", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/sms"},
  {"file": "f609_2.jpg", "caption": "The Eid offer sent, with who got it", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/sms/1"},
  {"file": "f609_3.jpg", "caption": "A promoter's card: link, share, order earned and the payout choices", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/affiliates"}],
 ["Built this round. The texts go out through whichever SMS service the owner connected in Connections (the same one used for order messages); in this test they went through the test gateway, so NOT verified: delivery to a real phone and the real gateway's own limits. Money to promoters is paid by the owner outside the site and written down here; nothing is sent to any payment service."])

w(612, "Built and tested this round, with both real programs running side by side on this computer and driven by hand in the browser: this site, and the real PharmaTrack project (the folder pharmacy-stock-management-main, on a throw-away copy of its database). PharmaTrack was given what it lacked: a stock ledger, counter sales, stock counts and the link itself. The pictures below are the whole run in order, 30 steps, each taken from the owner's Chrome: joining the programs, a count, a counter sale, goods given back, goods received, a correction on the site, an online order, the site switched off and on again, the short list, and a stock difference found and put right.",
 ["Joining: on this site the PharmaTrack card got an address and a key; on PharmaTrack the sync screen's Test button answered 'the e-commerce site answered and accepted the key'; Match medicines linked Seclo and Tuska by name, strength and company, and REFUSED to link Napa 500 mg because a box holds 30 or 510 pieces on the site and 40 in PharmaTrack (it would have been a wrong quantity)",
  "Master Stock Sync was switched on in PharmaTrack; a stock count of 31 boxes of Seclo (12 strips of 10) was saved there and matched the site's 31",
  "A shop sale made on PharmaTrack's counter screen (2 strips of Seclo, 120 taka) took 20 pieces off the site's stock too: 31 boxes became 30.8333 (20 of 120 pieces)",
  "A correction made on this site's stock screen (30 boxes, broken) reached PharmaTrack as a movement of the other program; a finished online order of 1 box took 120 pieces off PharmaTrack's shelf with the price converted to a price per piece",
  "A deliberately lost message was caught: Compare stock listed Seclo as 3575 here and 3600 on the site, with the difference, and said to count the side that is right; with nothing wrong it said both shelves agree",
  "Run again in the owner's own Chrome with both programs open in two tabs (count, counter sale, goods given back, goods received, a correction on the site, the site switched off then on, a medicine marked Not available): every change reached the other side, once; with the site down a sale still completed, was shown as failed with the reason, and the scheduler sent it by itself on its second try (about two minutes later)",
  "Found by that run and fixed: a restored or reset PharmaTrack database starts its sale numbers again, and the site silently dropped the repeated reference as 'already applied' (a sale was lost without any sign); references now carry the time, and a 'duplicate' answer is written on the message so it can never pass unseen",
  "Found by that run and added: when Compare stock shows a difference there are now two buttons per medicine, 'this shelf is right: set the site to it' and 'the site is right: set this shelf to it', each tried live and each leaving the two shelves equal",
  "A medicine marked Not available on the site appeared on PharmaTrack's own short-list page (with its notification), and the API answered 401 without or with a wrong key, 422 for a bad message, 'duplicate' for a repeated reference and 'unknown' for a name it cannot place",
  "Found by doing it and fixed: a box that cannot hold one piece of 120 exactly made the two shelves drift by 0.004 of a piece with every change; quantities now travel as whole pieces and a figure a hair from a whole piece is that piece, and Compare ignores less than half a piece",
  "On PharmaTrack: every change is one row in pieces (never edited), sales are never refused for lack of recorded stock (the figure may go below nothing and is flagged), goods given back go on the shelf and never more than was sold, goods received on an order go onto the shelf, and a sale made while the site is down is kept and sent again later with a growing wait",
  "Every message both ways is applied once (the same reference again is a duplicate), a wrong key is 401, and while Master Stock Sync is off PharmaTrack answers 409 so the site keeps the message; addresses must be https on a public site (plain localhost only in the local environment)",
  "Automatic tests: 13 new here, and 55 new in PharmaTrack (ledger 10, sync 24, short list 10, screens 11); the full suites pass (2291 here, 442 in PharmaTrack)"],
 [{"file": "f612_live01.jpg", "caption": "Before the test: the site holds 28.583 boxes of Seclo 20 mg", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live02.jpg", "caption": "PharmaTrack sync screen before anything is joined (Master Stock Sync off)", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live03.jpg", "caption": "Test connection: the site answered and accepted the key", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live04.jpg", "caption": "Match medicines: 1 of 1 linked; the site medicines PharmaTrack does not have are listed", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live05.jpg", "caption": "Master Stock Sync switched on: One stock is running", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live06.jpg", "caption": "Stock count form: 28 boxes and 7 strips counted", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /stock"},
  {"file": "f612_live07.jpg", "caption": "Count saved: PharmaTrack shows 28 boxes 7 strips (3,430 pieces)", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /stock"},
  {"file": "f612_live08.jpg", "caption": "Counter sale: 3 strips of Seclo at 60 taka, 180 taka", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /shop-sales/create"},
  {"file": "f612_live09.jpg", "caption": "Sale S000001 saved in PharmaTrack", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /shop-sales/1"},
  {"file": "f612_live10.jpg", "caption": "The site now shows 28.333 boxes (30 pieces came off)", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live11.jpg", "caption": "Goods given back: 10 pieces taken back on sale S000001", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /shop-sales/1"},
  {"file": "f612_live12.jpg", "caption": "The site now shows 28.417 boxes (10 pieces came back)", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live13.jpg", "caption": "Goods received: add 1 box, reason new goods arrived", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /stock"},
  {"file": "f612_live14.jpg", "caption": "PharmaTrack now shows 29 boxes 5 strips", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /stock"},
  {"file": "f612_live15.jpg", "caption": "The site now shows 29.417 boxes (the box was added there too)", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live16.jpg", "caption": "On the site: a stock correction to 29 boxes, reason broken", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live17.jpg", "caption": "The correction saved on the site (its movement list)", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live18.jpg", "caption": "PharmaTrack follows: it now shows 29 boxes", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /stock"},
  {"file": "f612_live19.jpg", "caption": "A finished online order on the site: 1 box of Seclo", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/orders/339"},
  {"file": "f612_live20.jpg", "caption": "PharmaTrack shows 28 boxes: the online order took 1 box off its shelf too", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /stock"},
  {"file": "f612_live21.jpg", "caption": "With the site switched off, a counter sale of 5 strips still completes (S000002)", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /shop-sales/2"},
  {"file": "f612_live22.jpg", "caption": "The sync screen shows that sale as failed, could not reach the site, beside the messages that did arrive", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live23.jpg", "caption": "The site is back: the scheduler sent the sale again by itself (2 tries) and every row is done", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live24.jpg", "caption": "The site now shows 27.583 boxes (the delayed sale arrived)", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_live25.jpg", "caption": "On the site: an ordered medicine, before staff choose", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/orders/169"},
  {"file": "f612_live26.jpg", "caption": "Staff mark the medicine Not available", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/orders/169"},
  {"file": "f612_live27.jpg", "caption": "It appears on PharmaTrack's own short list, with a notification", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /shortlist"},
  {"file": "f612_live28.jpg", "caption": "Compare stock finds a real difference: 3,285 here, 3,310 on the site, 25 apart", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live29.jpg", "caption": "Fix: this shelf is right, so the site is told to set itself to it", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_live30.jpg", "caption": "The site now shows 27.375 boxes (3,285 pieces): the two shelves agree again", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/stock/medicines/22873"},
  {"file": "f612_1.jpg", "caption": "This site's PharmaTrack screen: every message, a refused one kept with a retry", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/pharmatrack"},
  {"file": "f612_2.jpg", "caption": "This site's PharmaTrack card in Connections", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/connections"}],
 ["Done for this site and for PharmaTrack (uncommitted in both). Honest limits: the programs were joined over http on one computer (the local environment allows that; production needs https on a public address), PharmaTrack ran on a throw-away database with three medicines, and an accepted round trip over the internet between two deployed servers was not tried. Matching about 26,000 medicines took about 20 seconds, so it now runs in the background with a progress note. A positive stock change from PharmaTrack needs the medicine to have a purchase on this site already (it needs a cost); otherwise the line is reported, not invented. Not built: linking a medicine by hand when names differ, and a screen to correct the PharmaTrack opening stock in one go."])

w(613, "Built and tested this round. A provider (Rahim) opened Sell > Services, made Maths and physics lesson (60 minutes, 500 taka, Mirpur) and gave it three daily times with two places each. A buyer opened the service, took the second time, gave a name, a phone and a note, and asked for it. The provider saw the request and pressed Confirm; the buyer's private page then showed Confirmed with the provider's phone.",
 ["The provider adds a service with a name, how long it takes, the price, the area, and times (one, or the same time every day for a number of days); each time has a number of places",
  "The service page lists the free times; a buyer picks one and asks without signing up, and gets a private page (a link nobody can guess) that shows waiting, then confirmed or declined, and can cancel before the cut-off hours set in Settings",
  "The provider sees each request with the buyer's name, phone and note, and Confirm, Decline (with a reason the buyer is told) and later Done; a time with all places taken cannot be booked and a request that waits too long is declined by itself",
  "The provider sees the buyer's phone with the request, and the buyer sees the provider's phone only after Confirm; the same phone cannot ask for the same time twice (but may ask again after a decline); the owner can hide a service and its bookings stay",
  "The provider is messaged about a new request; a signed-in buyer is messaged when it is confirmed or declined and once the day before (27 automatic tests)"],
 [{"file": "f613_1.jpg", "caption": "The provider's service page with its times and a waiting request", "role": "wholesale", "url": "/wholesale/sell/services"},
  {"file": "f613_2.jpg", "caption": "The buyer's private page after the provider confirmed", "role": "visitor", "url": "/services/booking/{link}"}],
 ["Built this round from the spec extras list. Payment is not taken on the site: it is paid to the provider when they meet, and the page says so. A buyer who is not signed in is not messaged (they keep the private link), which is the one gap. While testing, three confirmation messages were found to show in English on the Bangla page; fixed and translated."])

w(577, "Built and tested this round as the placeholder the spec asks for. A signed-in buyer opened the Prescription marketplace page, read what it will be, and added their name, phone and area to the list of people who want it. The owner opened the list in the back office.",
 ["The public page explains the idea in three steps (send your prescription, pharmacies answer with a price, you choose) and says it is coming; it asks for a phone number and optionally a name and area; a signed-in person's name and phone are filled in",
  "After signing up the page says thanks and that they are on the list; signing up again with the same number does not make a second row",
  "The back office list (for those who manage customers) shows how many people want it, with name, phone, area and when, and how many prescriptions and answers exist so far (none yet)",
  "The tables for a prescription request and a pharmacy's answer are ready for the real marketplace, but nothing creates them yet; the sign-up is rate-limited (6 automatic tests)"],
 [{"file": "f577_1.jpg", "caption": "Tell me when it opens: the form", "role": "admin", "url": "/prescription-market"},
  {"file": "f577_2.jpg", "caption": "Done: thanks and on the list", "role": "admin", "url": "/prescription-market"},
  {"file": "f577_3.jpg", "caption": "The owner's list of people who want it", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/rx-market"}],
 ["A stub on purpose (spec: Prescription marketplace stub, Future). The marketplace itself, with pharmacies answering prescriptions, is not built."])

w(17, "Built and tested this round as an installable app for suppliers. A supplier (Rahim Traders) opened the Supplier app page: the count of orders waiting for them in large type, then one list of their tools (orders for their products, their products, offers and bundles, services, price requests, buyers' questions and more). The page carries its own app manifest so the phone can install it as a separate app.",
 ["/supplier shows who the seller is, how many orders wait for them in large type, and one list of their own tools; it serves a seller, a restaurant owner, an MPO and a craftsman, each seeing only their own screens",
  "The page has its own manifest (name, start page /supplier, its own id), so a phone installs it as a second app next to the shop, with the same icons; checked over a normal server where the manifest answers as application/manifest+json",
  "Buyers, staff and the owner have no supplier app (a plain 404 page), a signed-out visitor is asked to sign in, and a suspended seller has none (9 automatic tests)"],
 [{"file": "f17_1.jpg", "caption": "The supplier app's first screen", "role": "wholesale", "url": "/supplier"}],
 ["The app is a web app that installs to the phone's home screen (PWA), not a store app: no Play Store or App Store listing was built, and the spec's separate store apps would be a further project. The plain PHP test server used here cannot serve a file name ending in .webmanifest, so the manifest was checked on artisan serve and is fine on a normal web server."])

w(18, "Built and tested together with item 17. The supplier app and the shop use the same account and the same sign-in, so a supplier signs in once. The shop's menu has a link to the supplier app for suppliers, and the supplier app has a link back to the shop.",
 ["One account for both: the supplier app needs no second sign-in because it is part of the same site and the same session",
  "A seller sees a way across to the supplier app in the shop's menu and footer; the supplier app has a link back to the shop",
  "Someone who does not sell is never shown the way across, and one login serves both apps (two automatic tests)"],
 [{"file": "f17_1.jpg", "caption": "The supplier app, with its way back to the shop", "role": "wholesale", "url": "/supplier"},
  {"file": "f17_3.jpg", "caption": "Phone notifications: the inbox offers them, and says how to allow them when the browser has blocked them", "role": "paikari", "url": "/inbox"},
  {"file": "f17_2.jpg", "caption": "Connections: Web Push makes its own signing keys when switched on", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/connections"}],
 ["Phone and browser notifications (Web Push) were built with this: the owner only switches the card on, the site makes its own signing keys, and a person says yes once on their own device; the Messages screen has a Push tick per message. NOT verified live: a notification arriving on a real phone or browser, because this test browser blocks notifications and there is no push service reachable here; the sending was tested in 18 automatic tests with a fake sender, and the toggle's blocked state was seen on screen."])

w(55, "Checked together with item 612: PharmaTrack and this site were joined and one stock was followed through a count, a shop sale, a correction, an online order and a deliberate difference, all by hand in the browser.",
 ["Sales, returns, receipts, corrections, counts and online orders made on either side reach the other, once, in pieces",
  "Medicines are matched by name, strength and company, and never linked when the pieces in a box differ",
  "Compare stock shows any difference and changes nothing"],
 [{"file": "f612_5.jpg", "caption": "PharmaTrack's sync screen", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"},
  {"file": "f612_9.jpg", "caption": "Compare stock", "role": "admin", "url": "PharmaTrack /sync"}],
 ["Details and honest limits in item 612."])

w(138, "Opened an order in the back office and marked a line Not available. With the PharmaTrack connection on, the medicine is also sent to PharmaTrack's short list.",
 ["Staff can mark a medicine \"Not available\" while checking an order, and the order total drops by that line",
  "The medicine is sent once to PharmaTrack's short list (when the link is on and Live), never twice, and never stops the check if PharmaTrack is down (item 612)",
  "The record of medicines asked for but not available is also kept on the Price requests and Reports pages"],
 [{"file": "f138_1.jpg", "caption": "An order being checked: Full, Partial or Not available", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/orders/168"},
  {"file": "f612_1.jpg", "caption": "The message about it on the PharmaTrack screen", "role": "admin", "url": "/admin/pharmatrack"}],
 ["The short list is PharmaTrack's own list; this site adds to it and does not read it back."])

print("written")
